'''''Begonia obliqua''''' is the [[type species]] of the genus ''[[Begonia]]''<ref>Linnaeus, Species Plantarum 2:1056. 1753</ref> and the species to which Plumier first gave the name ''Begonia''. It is native to [[Martinique]], [[Dominica]], and [[Guadeloupe]].

The name has been misapplied to ''[[Begonia grandis]]'' by [[Carl Peter Thunberg|Thunberg]], to ''Begonia minor'' by [[Charles Louis L'Héritier de Brutelle|L'Héritier]], and to ''Begonia fischeri'' by [[José Mariano de Conceição Vellozo|Vellozo]].

